   "reading": "PAR2 was triggered by 66.3 mm2. Return is 52.9 of the 924.3, so removing it ENTIRELY still leaves 13.4 mm2 over: return alone could not have avoided PAR2 at S58. The binding terms are the 465.5 mm2 fixed debit (287 mm2 of it an unmapped legacy complement) and 721 padding sites (power-of-two NP)."
  }
 },
 "minimal_return": {
  "rule": "Little's law: entries = arrival rate x residence time. With credits a node side needs rate (1/cycle) x credit round trip (4 cycles) = 4 entries; the backlog then waits at its source pair, which holds one round (8 rows) and gets one more round of buffer so its next round can start. Without credits, the most that can ever be live is every partial of the rounds in flight: NP x 8 x 65 bits a round.",
  "designs": {
   "NP4096_R128": {
    "current_bits": 69771008,
    "current_mm2": 52.9,
    "credit_bits": 9001728,
    "credit_mm2": 6.82,
    "two_round_envelope_bits": 6406144,
    "two_round_envelope_mm2": 4.86,
    "burst_per_root_per_round": 256,
    "round_cycles_min": 40
   },
   "NP2048_R64": {
    "current_bits": 34885504,
    "current_mm2": 26.45,
    "credit_bits": 4500864,
    "credit_mm2": 3.41,
    "two_round_envelope_bits": 3203072,
    "two_round_envelope_mm2": 2.43,
    "burst_per_root_per_round": 256,
    "round_cycles_min": 40
   }
  },
  "latency_effect": "None priced: the drain rate is the same 1 result/cycle/root either way, and the model's issue term already paces matvecs to the result write (t_ret). Adoption still needs the RTL measurement AGENTS requires."
 },
